# VESTARV LOCAL DELTA (D5) -- harness build/run artefacts, see ../VENDORED.md.
#
# The suite COMPILES its test programs into this directory and names them
# "<target>_<program>-<misa>" with NO extension, e.g.
#     vesta_castalia_debug-40101107
#     vestaspike4_checksum-40001105
# so a scored run leaves a handful of unrelated-looking ELFs sitting next to
# the vendored sources.  They are outputs, not code, and none of them belongs
# in the repository.
#
# Listed by SHAPE rather than by name because the misa suffix changes with the
# target and the program list grows.
# The program list is longer than it first looks (download programs even carry
# a random suffix: vestaspike4_download_wxzqyam0-40001105), so this matches the
# SHAPE of every one of them -- any name ending in "-" plus an 8-hex-digit misa
# value -- rather than enumerating programs that will keep being added.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]
logs/
__pycache__/
